    {
      "text": "Replacing approximately 20% of the Mo with V will improve the room-temperature compressive strength–plasticity balance.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Replacing Mo with V lowers the alloy's overall electronegativity difference.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed substitution will preserve a disordered BCC structure.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed substitution will maintain substantial lattice distortion and solution strengthening.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A larger electronegativity difference produces a larger strengthening effect through greater complexity of local environments.",
