      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6504951::web::021::property_targeted_quantitative_design_of"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lowering the electronegativity difference reduces bond stiffening.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reduced bond stiffening lowers the barrier to dislocation motion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Greater dislocation mobility will enhance plastic deformation without significantly reducing solution strengthening.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The V-modified alloy will retain a compressive yield strength near 1700 MPa.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The V-modified alloy will reach or exceed 15% room-temperature compressive plastic strain before failure.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Arc melting followed by homogenization at about 1400°C for 12 hours and rapid quenching will retain the disordered BCC structure.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The beneficial effect requires retaining enough Mo to avoid excessively diminishing solution strengthening.",
